.TH TUMMLER 1 "2026-10-22" "tummler 0.3.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tummler \- mix any file into any format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tummler
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I INPUT\fR...
[\fIFORMAT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
tummler converts files by putting the target format last:
.PP
.RS
tummler photo.png jpg
.RE
.PP
Native Rust for images, spreadsheets and archives.
ffmpeg for audio/video and HEIC/AVIF.
pandoc for documents.
poppler (\fBpdftoppm\fR / \fBpdftotext\fR) for PDF as input.
LibreOffice (\fBsoffice\fR) is used only if already on PATH; tummler never installs it.
.PP
The last argument is the format if it is a known extension.
.B \-\-
separates files whose names start with
.BR \- .
.B \-
means stdin/stdout.
.SH INSTALL
Binary from GitHub Releases (no Rust):
.PP
.RS
curl \-fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RUdolf1517/tummler/main/install.sh | sh
.RE
.PP
Homebrew. This is a third\-party tap, not homebrew/core.
The repository is not named
.BR homebrew\-tummler ,
so the tap needs an explicit URL.
Homebrew 6+ requires
.B tap trust
(see
.I https://docs.brew.sh/Tap-Trust
).
A fully qualified formula name trusts only that formula:
.PP
.RS
brew tap RUdolf1517/tummler https://github.com/RUdolf1517/tummler
.br
brew install RUdolf1517/tummler/tummler
.RE
.PP
To install by short name, trust the formula first:
.PP
.RS
brew trust \-\-formula RUdolf1517/tummler/tummler
.br
brew install tummler
.RE
.PP
Do not
.B brew trust RUdolf1517/tummler
unless you accept every current and future formula in the tap.
Intel Mac is bottled (
.B tummler-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " EXT" "\fR, \fB\-\-format=" EXT
Target format explicitly.
.TP
.BI \-o " PATH" "\fR, \fB\-\-output=" PATH
Output file or directory.
.B \-
is stdout.
.TP
.BI \-q " N" "\fR, \fB\-\-quality=" N
Lossy quality 1–100.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite\fR, \fB\-\-force
Replace existing files.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Walk directories. Does not follow symbolic links.
.TP
.B \-\-preserve\-structure
With
.B \-r
and
.B \-o
directory, keep subdirectories:
.I photos/vacation/photo.jpg
→
.I out/vacation/photo.webp .
Default flattens to the output directory.
Ignored without
.B \-r
and an
.B \-o
directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-include " GLOB
Keep matching files (repeatable). Matches name or path.
.B *
does not cross
.BR / ;
.B **
does (e.g.
.B **/.git/**
).
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " GLOB
Drop matching files (repeatable). Same glob rules as
.BR \-\-include .
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-newer
Skip if the output exists and is not older than the input.
.TP
.B \-\-preserve\-mtime
Copy the input modification time onto the output (like
.BR cp " " \-p ).
Ignored for stdin/stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " STR
Prepend to the output stem.
.TP
.BI \-\-suffix " STR
Append to the output stem:
.B photo.png webp \-\-suffix _opt
→
.IR photo_opt.webp .
No path separators. Ignored with
.B \-o
file or stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-max " PX
Longest side in pixels (images/video). Never upscales.
.TP
.BI \-\-resize " SPEC
.BR 50% ", " 800x ", " x600 ", or " 800x600
(images/video). Aspect kept.
.TP
.BI \-\-page " N
PDF page (1-based). Default: all pages stacked in one image.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-meta
Drop EXIF/GPS and author tags.
ffmpeg uses
.B \-map_metadata \-1
(including remux).
pandoc clears title/author/date.
Images already drop EXIF on convert.
LibreOffice and a PDF copy are unchanged.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS
Kill that file's converter after
.I SECS
(ffmpeg, pandoc, pdftoppm, soffice). Default: no limit.
On timeout: kill the process group, log on stderr, continue the batch.
Summary shows
.BR timed\ out ;
exit 1.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs =\fIN
Parallel jobs. 0 means the number of CPUs (media capped at 2).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Errors only.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the plan, write nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN
auto, always, or never.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Same as
.BR \-\-color=never .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-info
About tummler.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-formats
Supported formats.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-deps
Status of ffmpeg, pandoc, poppler, soffice.
In a TTY, offer to install ffmpeg/pandoc/poppler (never LibreOffice).
.B \-y
installs without asking.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-auto\-install
Do not offer to install missing tools.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Install missing tools without prompting.
.TP
.BI \-\-sheet " NAME|N
Spreadsheet sheet: name or 1-based index. First sheet by default.
.B *
means every sheet, each to its own file.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-sheets
Every sheet →
.I table\-Sheet1.csv
(and so on).
.TP
.BI \-\-ffmpeg\-args " ARGS
Extra ffmpeg arguments.
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " SHELL
Print a completion script: bash, zsh, fish, powershell, elvish.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Print this man page (groff) to stdout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Conversion failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (Ctrl\-C). Child ffmpeg/pandoc/pdftoppm processes are killed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
tummler photo.png jpg
.TQ
tummler photo.png jpeg \-q 80
.TQ
tummler icon.svg png
.TQ
tummler photo.heic jpg \-\-max 1920
.TQ
tummler ./photos webp \-r \-\-skip\-newer \-o ./out
.TQ
tummler ./photos webp \-r \-o ./out \-\-preserve\-structure
.TQ
tummler photo.png jpg \-\-preserve\-mtime
.TQ
tummler photo.png webp \-\-suffix _opt
.TQ
tummler ./photos webp \-r \-\-timeout 120
.TQ
tummler table.xlsx csv
.TQ
tummler table.csv xlsx
.TQ
tummler report.docx pdf
.TQ
tummler report.pdf png
.TQ
tummler report.pdf png \-\-page 2
.TQ
tummler report.pdf docx
.TQ
tummler video.mkv mp4 \-\-strip\-meta
.TQ
tummler \-\-check\-deps
.TQ
tummler slides.pptx pdf
.TQ
cat in.png | tummler \- jpeg > out.jpeg
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B ffmpeg
Audio, video, HEIC, AVIF, lossy WebP.
.TP
.B pandoc
Documents. A pandoc PDF needs LaTeX.
.TP
.B poppler
.B pdftoppm
(PDF → image, all pages stacked; \-\-page N for one) and
.B pdftotext
(PDF → text / docx fallback).
.TP
.B soffice
Optional. Slides, and Word/PDF layout when already installed. Never auto-installed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color when set (non-empty).
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
disables color.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR pandoc (1),
.BR pdftoppm (1),
.BR pdftotext (1),
.BR soffice (1),
.BR brew (1)
